Native Windows (MSVC) build of REBOUNDx 5.1.0 against the REBOUND PyPI wheel.
The C fixes (VLAs, rand_r) are the same fix as the unmerged upstream PR
https://github.com/dtamayo/reboundx/pull/170 (consulted as a reference). The setup.py mechanism differs:
pure-Python PE/COFF parsing instead of dumpbin, get_export_symbols override instead of a PyInit stub.
The src/steppers.c shim is new; PR 170 does not touch that file.
Changes: setup.py (import library for librebound generated from its export table, .def export
file generated from the compiled objects, no rpath on Windows, no PyInit export),
reboundx/__init__.py (import rebound before loading libreboundx), src/gr_full.c and
src/interpolation.c (C99 VLAs -> malloc/free), src/stochastic_forces.c (rand_r shim),
src/steppers.c (reb_integrator_ias15/whfast are not exported from REBOUND's Windows DLL).

